    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1267">

                <pb facs="1111" n="797" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg797"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72116/40</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Germany</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gerard</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-09-18T12:00:00-05:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">September 18, 1914, 12 noon</hi>.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>191. Just received telegram referring to dumdum bullets. While you could not
                    refuse to send specimens if requested the Government will of course understand
                    that no action will be taken by this Government <pb facs="1112" n="798"
                        xml:id="pg798"/> in the matter. The President’s answer to the Emperor will
                    cover all matters of this kind. He hears whatever is said but does not discuss
                    the merits of the controversy and your action in refusing to be drawn into the
                    discussion of such questions is approved.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W.J.Bryan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
